  "description": "Pad variable-length token sequences to a common length and produce a mask distinguishing real tokens from padding.",
  "theory": "## Understanding the Theory: Pad Sequences and Build Attention Mask\n\n### Core Intuition: Why Do We Need This?\n**Pad Sequences and Build Attention Mask** represents a fundamental data modeling and statistical reasoning technique in **NLP Fundamentals Sprint**. In enterprise machine learning, quantitative analytics, and decision science, algorithms must handle asynchronous logs, missing observations, skewed class distributions, and high-cardinality partitions. A mathematically rigorous implementation guarantees statistically unbiased estimates and idempotent transformations.\n\nUnderstanding the core mechanics enables engineers to diagnose convergence anomalies, optimize memory layouts, and construct maintainable ML pipelines from first principles.\n\n### Mathematical Principles & Formulation\nThe operation is governed by the following mathematical formulation:\n\n$$\nM_{ij} = \\begin{cases} 0 & \\text{if } x_{ij} \\ne \\text{PAD} \\\\ -\\infty & \\text{if } x_{ij} = \\text{PAD} \\end{cases}\n$$\n\nIn this formulation:\n* The input features and parameters are projected, normalized, or aggregated according to established algorithmic invariants.\n* Dimensional consistency is preserved across all tensor or matrix axes, ensuring mathematical validity.\n* Intermediate accumulators maintain numerical dynamic range to protect against floating-point anomalies.\n\n### Step-by-Step Computational Workflow\n1. **Phase 1: Input Validation & Dimension Setup**: Validate input array dimensions, check for empty sequences or invalid bounds, and convert inputs into contiguous buffers.\n2. **Phase 2: Core Algorithmic Transformation**: Execute the foundational mathematical logic using vectorized SIMD array operations or optimized iteration.\n3. **Phase 3: Aggregation & Normalization**: Compute required sums, projections, or ranking reductions while guarding against division by zero.\n4. **Phase 4: Output Assembly & Precision Guarantee**: Format outputs into required data types and verify that returned numerical estimates adhere to expected precision thresholds.\n\n### Practical Machine Learning Applications & Nuances\n* **Statistical Unbiasedness & Degrees of Freedom**: Applying proper Bessel corrections and degrees of freedom safeguards sample statistics against systemic sample bias.\n* **Vectorized Array Operations**: Leveraging contiguous columnar execution avoids slow Python interpreter loop overhead when evaluating million-row datasets.\n* **Null Safety & Edge Case Handling**: Explicit handling of missing data, empty partitions, and single-value inputs prevents runtime exceptions in production batch pipelines.\n* **Algorithmic Complexity**: Operates with optimal asymptotic time and space complexity, ensuring minimal compute overhead.",
